   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1941-01-02">January 2, 1941.</date></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                  Tillich</rs>,</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>As I am running downstairs to post an order for 30 copies of your WAR AIMS, I want to
               take this opportunity to thank you for your courtesy in giving me the two copies, and
               also to tell you how much I appreciate your INTERPRETATION OF HISTORY – such parts as
               I have read! I only began it since returning from Christmas holidays.</p>
            <p>I am going to see that quite a few people at Teachers College get copies – <rs
                  ref="#tillich_person_id__4127" type="person">Dr. Goodwin Watson</rs> –(for whom I
               happen to be doing this paper) – <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4128" type="person">Dr.
                  Ernest Johnson</rs> and a number of others. Also, some prominent Chinese leaders.
               (As I am a missionary from <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__738" type="place"
               >China</rs>.)</p>
            <p>I am indeed grateful to my friend, <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4129" type="person">Miss Scudder</rs>, for 
            sending me this copy. (She despairs of converting me to Pacifism, however!)</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Gratefully,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4126" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Alice Gregg</hi></rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
